      "source": [
        "## Task 10 — Speeding ticket function\n",
        "\n",
        "**Question:** Implement `caught_speeding(speed, is_birthday)` using these rules:\n",
        "- Speed up to and including 60 mph: `\"No Ticket\"`\n",
        "- Speed 61–80 mph: `\"Small Ticket\"`\n",
        "- Speed 81 mph or higher: `\"Big Ticket\"`\n",
        "- On a birthday, allow 5 mph more.\n",
        "\n",
        "A simple way to apply the birthday allowance is to subtract 5 from the recorded speed before checking the usual thresholds."
      ],
      "id": "y7W4efQVRuom"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 10,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "mSOgSxc0Ruom",
        "outputId": "99e8dae6-81ed-4deb-bbaf-f536b3f1ceca",
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/"
        }
      },
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": [
            "Q10 test 1: No Ticket\n",
            "Q10 test 2: Small Ticket\n",
            "Q10 test 3: Big Ticket\n",
            "Q10 birthday boundary: No Ticket\n"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "source": [
        "def caught_speeding(speed, is_birthday):\n",
        "    allowance = 5 if is_birthday else 0\n",
        "    adjusted_speed = speed - allowance\n",
        "\n",
        "    if adjusted_speed <= 60:\n",
        "        return \"No Ticket\"\n",
        "    elif adjusted_speed <= 80:\n",
        "        return \"Small Ticket\"\n",
        "    else:\n",
        "        return \"Big Ticket\"\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"Q10 test 1:\", caught_speeding(60, False))   # No Ticket\n",
        "print(\"Q10 test 2:\", caught_speeding(75, True))    # Small Ticket\n",
        "print(\"Q10 test 3:\", caught_speeding(85, False))   # Big Ticket\n",
        "print(\"Q10 birthday boundary:\", caught_speeding(65, True))  # No Ticket"
      ],
      "id": "mSOgSxc0Ruom"
    },
